From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:02:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/49] moe cache: the release in-place prefill (TODO #317)
 stands down when a sparse table exists

With any sparse (mmap) table, moe_cache_get_table answers from the tier code, which
refuses a remap published without a freshness round; pf_in_place_locked sets none.
Only reachable with a GTT arena (APU) and mixed tables; inert on discrete GPUs.

(cherry picked from commit 89cf15085fd10300e6ce42f1f69461e412ccb41a)
(cherry picked from commit 31d09ae565394c20296f6bf86884f02efe95641b)
(cherry picked from commit 774a9afc76ace225605b0462629eccb48a796f5c)
(cherry picked from commit 215542855ab6be0a5caf0252ec2ab8b7cfe48402)
(cherry picked from commit b529c3c3a8b22392a562c98bd76c279c9db89967)
(cherry picked from commit f614a0a8b781764c37da5923961d16f3cda87d7d)
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu
index 02376a59a2..f4d34a2031 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/moe-expert-cache.cu
@@ -12018,7 +12018,10 @@ bool moe_cache_update_host(const ggml_tensor * weight, const ggml_tensor * weigh
         // and this arm is INERT (never wrong -- the seed and this path are otherwise independent).
         t.remap_n_used  = 0;
         t.remap_prefill = false;
-        if (pf_in_place_locked(t, table, weight_cpy, device, ids, n_used, n_tok, ids_nb0, ids_nb1, stream)) {
+        // ours: with any sparse (mmap) table, moe_cache_get_table answers from our tier, which refuses a remap without a
+        // freshness round (remap_round); this publish sets none, so stand the release in-place prefill down.
+        if (!g_any_sparse &&
+            pf_in_place_locked(t, table, weight_cpy, device, ids, n_used, n_tok, ids_nb0, ids_nb1, stream)) {
             t.taken_cpy = weight_cpy;   // TODO #335/#336: the promise this hook makes to the scheduler
             return true;   // the op reads the arena; no copy of the used residents is made at all
         }
